Fix softbuffer's Wayland SW buffer allocation on illumos.

softbuffer (pop-os fork, tag cosmic-4.0, rev c2b2c19) already uses POSIX
shm_open on the non-linux/non-freebsd path in create_memfile() -- it is NOT a
memfd_create gap. The real defect on illumos is the shm object NAME: softbuffer
builds it as "softbuffer-XXXXXXX" with no leading slash. illumos shm_open(3C)
requires the name to begin with "/" and rejects any other name with EINVAL
(errno 22). That is the exact panic COSMIC apps hit at
src/wayland/buffer.rs:52 -- "Failed to create POSIX shm to store buffer:
Os { code: 22, kind: InvalidInput }".

Verified with a C repro on the target: shm_open("/name", O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_EXCL,
0600) -> valid fd + ftruncate ok; shm_open("name", ...) -> EINVAL(22).

Fix (illumos/non-linux branch only):
  - prepend "/" to the shm name (the leading slash illumos requires).
  - drop the exec bit from the mode: Mode::RWXU (0700) -> Mode::RUSR|Mode::WUSR
    (0600), matching the proven cosmic-app-list / cosmic-applet-minimize illumos
    POSIX-shm idiom (rustix::fs::Mode::RUSR|WUSR). illumos accepts 0700 too, but
    0600 keeps the anonymous SW buffer non-executable and consistent.

This only touches the non-linux/freebsd branch, so Linux/FreeBSD (memfd) and
other targets are unchanged.

--- a/src/wayland/buffer.rs
+++ b/src/wayland/buffer.rs
@@ -37,7 +37,9 @@ fn create_memfile() -> File {
     let mut rng = fastrand::Rng::new();
 
     for _ in 0..=4 {
-        let mut name = String::from("softbuffer-");
+        // illumos shm_open(3C) requires the object name to begin with "/"
+        // (EINVAL otherwise). Prepend it here.
+        let mut name = String::from("/softbuffer-");
         name.extend(iter::repeat_with(|| rng.alphanumeric()).take(7));
         name.push('\0');
 
@@ -46,7 +48,8 @@ fn create_memfile() -> File {
         let fd = rustix::shm::shm_open(
             name,
             ShmOFlags::RDWR | ShmOFlags::CREATE | ShmOFlags::EXCL,
-            Mode::RWXU,
+            // 0600 (no exec bit) -- the proven illumos POSIX-shm mode.
+            Mode::RUSR | Mode::WUSR,
         );
         if !matches!(fd, Err(Errno::EXIST)) {
             let fd = fd.expect("Failed to create POSIX shm to store buffer.");
